# SESSION RHYTHM AND DELIVERABLES — TC ∥ DC

Canonical parallel contract for:

| Course | Repo | Final event theme |
| ------ | ---- | ----------------- |
| **Creativity Techniques (TC)** | `creativity-techniques-uem` | **What is creativity for you?** |
| **Digital Creativity (DC)** | `digital-creativity-uem` | **Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?** |

Official guía weights stay binding (TC **60/40**; DC **55/15/20/10** per current guía). This file is the **studio choreography** and intra-deliverable rubrics — it does not invent CONTENIDOS rows.

Keep this file **substance-aligned** across both repos when amended.

---

## 1. Lab vs Workshop — names are NOT swapped

| Name | What it is | What it is not |
| ---- | ---------- | -------------- |
| **Masterclass** | Professor slideshow: ideas + images (accepted Profield media) | Not the graded deliverable clock |
| **Lab (Portfolio)** | Exercises + debates that **must enter the portfolio** | Not free-time polish |
| **Workshop** | Protected studio time **from session 4** for **D2 Transposition** and **D3 final event** (≈ half / half) | Not a second lecture; **not** every-session filler; **not** D1 Analysis time |

Mnemonic: **Lab = leave traces in the portfolio. Workshop (from s4) = Transposition + final event — never D1.**

**D1 Analysis** is the next graded stake after early lessons, but it is defended in the **Analysis strip** (from session 3). It **does not** receive Workshop session time.

---

## 2. Mandatory session arc

### First lessons (sessions 1–3 · early units)

```text
[Analysis strip — rolling]
  Sessions 1–2: professor models how to analyse (lesson slideshow)
  From session 3: 2 students × ~15 min in-person defence each (D1)
         ↓
[Masterclass]  professor ideas + images (Profield under contract)
         ↓
[Lab · Portfolio]  exercises + debates  ← geometrical opener
         ↓
[Outro]  carry-forward — **no Workshop block**
```

**First-lesson law:** Do **not** invent Workshop slides, “studio piece this week,” or any side deliverable. First lessons end after Lab. Never invent graded work that is not on How to Pass.

### From session 4 (ordinary sessions with Workshop)

```text
[Analysis strip]  D1 defences continue as scheduled
         ↓
[Masterclass] → [Lab · Portfolio]
         ↓
[Workshop]  ≈ half **D2 Transposition** · ≈ half **D3 final event**  ← geometrical open + outro
```

Indicative 120 minutes:

| Block | ≈ minutes | First lessons (s1–s3) | From session 4 |
| ----- | --------- | --------------------- | -------------- |
| Analysis strip | 0–30 | Modelled analysis (s1–s2) or D1 defences (from s3) | D1 defences |
| Masterclass | 30–60 | Student deck · Profield images | Same |
| Lab (Portfolio) | 60–90 / 60–120 | Exercises → portfolio; **session ends here** | Exercises → portfolio |
| Workshop | — / 90–120 | **Absent** | ≈½ Transposition · ≈½ final event |

