## 3. Slideshow background law (programmatic)

| Slide role | Background |
| ---------- | ---------- |
| Masterclass idea / look / analyse / concept | Accepted **Profield** media (or course diagram) |
| **Lab opener** — “Exercises now — they go into your portfolio” | **Geometrical only** (`fractal-pass-track`) |
| Lab exercise slides (**exactly two** per unit) | Profield or plain text on theme |
| **Workshop opener** — from session 4 only (“Transposition / final event”) | **Geometrical only** |
| **Outro / carry-forward** | **Geometrical only** |
| Masterclass diagram fallback (no pack image) | **Koch triangle** (`generate-koch-triangle.mjs`) — not Sierpinski |

Never invent media. Never put Resource UUID / forger version in captions. Never use geometrical BGs as a substitute for required Profield slots on Masterclass content slides when a pack image exists.

Typed slide keys for forges / `content.json`:

```text
slide_role: unit_cover | analysis_opener | analysis_model | masterclass | lab_opener | lab_exercise | workshop_opener | workshop_work | outro
background_kind: profield | geometrical | diagram | none
portfolio_bound: true | false
```

`unit_cover` MUST open **Creativity Techniques** unit decks (title / stake); `analysis_opener` follows immediately. Digital Creativity may keep its existing cover slot naming. The student **lesson** (TC) MUST include Analysis method prose (not deck-only). `lab_opener` MUST appear **immediately before** the first `lab_exercise`. Forge **exactly two** `lab_exercise` slides per ordinary unit (lesson B2 matches).

