## 4. Five deliverables (parallel; course forks)

### D1 — Analysis (defence slideshow)

| | TC | DC |
| - | -- | -- |
| Object | Creativity / design artefact or campaign moment under brief | **Fashion image** related to a **piece on exhibition in Madrid** (coordinated visit with Spanish-cohort students) |
| Form | **15 min** in-person defence; support = **slideshow** | Same |
| Cadence | **2 students per session from session 3** | Same |
| Intra-rubric | Presentation **70%** · deliverable support **20%** · peer debate **10%** | Same |

### D2 — Transposition (critical review / palimpsest)

| | TC | DC |
| - | -- | -- |
| Object | **Free choice · free format** — discursive circulation as cultural feedback (palimpsest) | Transpose chosen material **into an image** (series OK) |
| Theory home | `DISCURSIVE-CIRCULATION-FORGE.mdc` (trans-unit) | Critical transposition + image ontology adjacency |
| Evidence | Source declaration + process trail + reading of **desajuste** production↔recognition | Source + image series + process trail |
| Required stakes | **Steimberg** genre/style/transposition · **Werhane & Bevan** moral imagination · **Munari** constraint/manifest practice (page-verify before Chicago) | Same ethical + circulation stakes; image ontology owns form |

This is the **critical review trans-unit** — not a fake CONTENIDOS ID; it is a
**course-wide deliverable** grounded in the masterclass forge. It sits inside
the **transversal CV critical layer** together with **C1–C3** (ideology;
labour; GenAI authorship): D2 owns circulation/moral imagination; C1–C3 own
soft-skill / labour / authorship framing. Neither is optional colour.

**Fail closed for D2 briefs:** missing triad location, missing desajuste
reading, or missing one of {Steimberg-grade transposition claim ·
Werhane-grade moral stake · Munari-grade method/manifest constraint} as a
named teaching question when Ahmes cites are still open.

### D3 — Atrium cohort event

| | Both |
| - | ---- |
| Venue | University **Atrio** — AV, lighting, PA, microphones |
| Submit | **Tech script** (cues, channels, roles, accessibility) |
| Live | Performance / defence of the work under the final event theme |
| TC theme | **What is creativity for you?** |
| DC theme | **Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?** |

### D4 — Portfolio index

Single index document containing:

1. Class **Lab** exercises (dated traces)  
2. **D1–D3** deliverables (or links + metadata)  
3. AI disclosure + authorship notes  

Without the index, exercises do not count as assembled evidence.

### D5 — Exam

| Part | Role |
| ---- | ---- |
| Test / questionnaire | Official knowledge instrument (maps to guía *pruebas*) |
| Final self-review | Written explanation of the **portfolio process** (oral may accompany) |

